# Line-ending policy for distributed scripts.
# PowerShell 5.1 mis-parses LF-only scripts (breaks backtick line-continuations),
# so .ps1 must be CRLF. Bash breaks on CRLF, so .sh must stay LF.
#
# Order matters: git applies the LAST matching line per attribute, and `*`
# matches everything — so the catch-all must come FIRST, with specific
# overrides listed AFTER it, or they get silently overridden.

*       text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
